"""
ARGYLE v0.5.0 - build hook.  Emits argyle_pkg.vhd (pure Python, no dependencies).

The tables were fitted to the source photo (WIN_20230207_23_50_54) in .heirloom_work/rb_argyle
(fold.py, ridgefit.py + lsfit.py, gfit.py, colfit_hw.py, mkdata.py) and are carried here as data.
The photo is one doubly periodic tile (524.8 px x 261.0 lines, fold residual 6 RGB rms):
  field  s = G(x) + H(y), G = the horizontal oscillator (even part GE + Pairs x odd part GO; the odd
         part makes every other diamond's core big / small), H = the vertical oscillator.
  colour R, B and the green ring envelope (base, amp) are smooth functions of (G shifted 15 px left,
         H) -- the composite chroma offset of the capture -- and green = base + amp * RING(s).

  C_GE    512 x 12 signed: GE over one cell (1024 = 1.0), index = phase bits 22..14.
  C_GO    256 x 12 signed: GO over the first half of the 2-cell period (the second half is -GO).
  C_HH    256 x 12 signed: H nodes over one row period (linear interpolation per line).
  C_RING  512 x 8 signed: the ring waveform over s = -2 .. 2 (1/128 steps).
  C_CT    1024 x 32: colour table, address = row(H, 32 rows from -31/32 in 1/16) & col(G, 32 cols
          from -1 in 1/16); word = R(8) & B(8) & BASE(8) & AMP(8, signed, amp/2).  RGB 0..255 as in the
          photo; the RTL converts to 10-bit YUV in the hardware convention (U = Cr, V = Cb).
"""
